_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Avoid forcing empty output/extract targets**

Calling `.output(self.output.clone().unwrap_or_default())` and `.extract_to(self.extract_to.clone().unwrap_or_default())` even when the options are `None` overrides the `Download` defaults with empty strings/path buffers. Because `Download::execute` interprets a present (even empty) `extract_to` as “use this path”, the extraction fallback to the downloaded file’s parent directory never runs, so archives end up unpacked in the process CWD instead of alongside the artifact. Apply the builder setters only when the caller actually configured them.

