_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Respect `case_sensitive` for glob checks.**

`case_sensitive = false` should let `Filter` match `foo.tar.gz` against `FOO.TAR.GZ`, but `glob_match` is still called with the original (mixed-case) values, so the match fails on case-sensitive filesystems. Normalize both the pattern and the haystack when the flag is off.

```diff
-        let matches_glob = self.globs.is_empty() || self.globs.iter().any(|g| glob_match(g, name));
+        let matches_glob = if self.globs.is_empty() {
+            true
+        } else if self.case_sensitive {
+            self.globs.iter().any(|g| glob_match(g, name))
+        } else {
+            let lowered_name = name.to_lowercase();
+            self.globs
+                .iter()
+                .any(|g| glob_match(&g.to_lowercase(), &lowered_name))
+        };
