_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Keep HEAD when we still need server-provided filenames**

We now skip the HEAD whenever `output` is `Some`, which also suppresses the probe when the caller passed a directory hint (e.g. `.output("/tmp/")` or an existing directory). In those cases we still rely on `Content-Disposition` to derive the filename; without it we now throw `DownloadError::NoFilename` or silently save CDN URLs like `...?download=` under the wrong name. Please only skip the HEAD when the caller supplied an explicit filename (not `"-"` and not a directory hint) and retain the existing HEAD path for directories. One way is to treat strings ending with `/` or resolving to an existing directory as “needs HEAD” before you branch. 
```diff
-        let (header_filename, url_filename) = if self.output.as_deref().is_none() {
+        let needs_head = match self.output.as_deref() {
+            None => true,
+            Some("-") => false,
+            Some(p) => {
+                let path = Path::new(p);
+                p.ends_with('/') || path.is_dir()
+            }
+        };
+
+        let (header_filename, url_filename) = if needs_head {
             let resp = Http::head(&self.url)?;
             (
                 resp.headers()
                     .get(CONTENT_DISPOSITION)
                     .and_then(filename_from_header),
                 filename_from_url(&self.url),
             )
         } else {
             (None, filename_from_url(&self.url))
         };
```

