_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Add context to migration errors for easier debugging.**

If a query fails (e.g., due to invalid JSON in a column), the error provides no indication of which column or query caused the failure. When migrating 9+ columns, this makes troubleshooting difficult.



<details>
<summary>Proposed improvement: Add error context</summary>

```diff
     let mut total = 0;
     for query in queries {
-        total += sql_query(&query).execute(conn)?;
+        total += sql_query(&query)
+            .execute(conn)
+            .map_err(|e| format!("Failed to execute migration query: {}\nError: {}", query, e))?;
     }
```

</details>


