In crates/soar-db/src/migration.rs around lines 141-144, the migration loop
executes raw SQL without adding any context to errors; update the loop to
enumerate the queries and wrap each execute call so any returned error is
augmented with contextual information (e.g., the failing query string and its
index/column name). Concretely, replace the bare sql_query(...).execute(conn)?
with a call that maps or converts the error to include format!("migration failed
for query #{}: {}", idx, query) (or use anyhow::Context::with_context) before
returning, so callers receive the original error plus the query/index that
caused it.
