_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Wrap migration queries in a transaction for atomicity.**

The function executes multiple UPDATE queries sequentially without an explicit transaction boundary. If a query fails mid-way (e.g., due to malformed JSON data), earlier queries have already committed, leaving some columns migrated to JSONB while others remain as text. This creates an inconsistent database state.

Consider wrapping all updates in a transaction to ensure all-or-nothing semantics.



<details>
<summary>Proposed fix: Add transaction boundary</summary>

```diff
+use diesel::connection::Connection;
