body:
_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**`std::thread::sleep` blocks the tokio worker thread.**

`install_single_package` is an `async fn` spawned via `tokio::spawn`. Using `std::thread::sleep` (line 1106) blocks the entire tokio worker thread, starving other concurrent installation tasks that share the same thread pool. Use `tokio::time::sleep` instead.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-                std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(500));
+                tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(500)).await;
```

This also requires changing the lock-acquisition loop to be `async`-compatible. Since `try_acquire` is sync, this is straightforward — only the sleep needs to be async.
</details>

