_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Unlink and link are separate transactions — crash between them leaves all variants unlinked.**

The unlink (line 89) and link (line 169) happen in separate DB transactions with filesystem operations in between. If any step between lines 92–166 fails (symlink creation, desktop integration, etc.), transaction 1 has already committed — all other variants are unlinked — but the selected variant is never linked. This leaves the package inoperable.

Consider wrapping the DB mutations in a single transaction, or at minimum, performing the link first (or using a compensating rollback on error).

