_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**`create_provide_symlinks` diverges from `bin_symlink_names()` for `target = Some, strategy = None`.**

Re-deriving the branch logic instead of calling `provide.bin_symlink_names()` has already caused a behavioral gap: when a provide has a `target` but no `strategy`, `bin_symlink_names()` (used by `remove_provide_symlinks`) resolves to `[name]`, but here neither the `target` branch (guarded by `provide.strategy.is_some()`) nor `needs_original_symlink` (which requires `(Some(_), Some(KeepBoth))` or `(None, _)`) matches — so **no symlink is created at all** for that provide. `from_string()` never produces this exact shape today, but `PackageProvide` is `Deserialize`, so any future/alternate construction path hitting it would silently install with a missing symlink while removal harmlessly no-ops looking for one that was never created.

