`compare_versions` returns `Equal` for two distinct commit hashes, but each hash still compares as `Less` or `Greater` against lexical version segments. This violates the `sort_by` comparator contract when both hashes are sorted with another version present, so the non-identical-hash case need a stable fallback such as lexical hash comparison, while `is_newer` can still treat different hashes as not newer each other.

